Imagine discovering that one of the world's most valuable domain names was accidentally available to buy. In 2015, former Google employee Sanmay Ved found google.com available for purchase, completed the transaction for just $12, and briefly became the owner of one of the internet's most iconic websites.

Instead of taking advantage of the mistake, Ved immediately contacted Google's security team and reported what had happened. The transaction was reversed within minutes, and his honesty earned widespread respect throughout the technology community.

Google rewarded Ved with more than $6,000 through its Vulnerability Reward Program. When he asked for the reward to be donated to the Art of Living schools in India, Google matched the amount, doubling the donation in recognition of his generosity.

This remarkable story proves that integrity is worth more than any unexpected opportunity. Doing the right thing, even when no one is watching, can create an impact far greater than personal gain and leave a legacy built on honesty and character.

